// @ens-test
// @exit 2
// @stderr-contains the test program stopped with code 1 while running 'first test exits'. Run that test alone with 'ens test --filter "first test exits"' to see its output
// A test program that ends with 1 before every result is in did not reach its own count of
// failures, so the command reports the stop and names the test it stopped in, rather than ending
// with 1 and no word of why.
